<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- 2026-08-20 — optional free-tier photo/icon-search API keys (Pixabay,
     Pexels, Unsplash, Flaticon — see ExternalApiClient.kt / ExternalModels.kt's
     header comments for the full multi-source fallback picture). All
     four are FREE to sign up for but do each require their own
     personal key, unlike every other provider in this project's search
     chains (Iconify, Openverse, Openclipart, Wikimedia Commons, Google's
     Material Icons metadata endpoint, and the DuckDuckGo scrape fallback
     all work with none of these four filled in).

     Left empty here on purpose — no placeholder/demo key is embedded in
     this project. ExternalApiClient.searchPhotos{Pixabay,Pexels,Unsplash}()
     and searchIconsFlaticon() each check their own key string first and
     skip the network call entirely (return an empty list, no request
     made) when it's blank, so leaving these empty is completely safe; it
     just means those chains rely on their key-less providers instead.

     To turn one on: sign up for a free key at the provider's own site,
     paste it in below, rebuild. Do NOT commit a real key to a public
     repo without checking that provider's terms on key exposure in a
     distributed app first.
       - Pixabay:  https://pixabay.com/api/docs/  (instant, no approval wait)
       - Pexels:   https://www.pexels.com/api/    (instant, no approval wait)
       - Unsplash: https://unsplash.com/developers (Demo tier, 50 req/hour)
       - Flaticon:  https://developer.flaticon.com/landing (instant free key) -->
<resources>
    <string name="pixabay_api_key" translatable="false"></string>
    <string name="pexels_api_key" translatable="false"></string>
    <string name="unsplash_access_key" translatable="false"></string>
    <string name="flaticon_api_key" translatable="false"></string>
</resources>
